Chapter: NaturalSize
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites Works chapter GopComposite
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 With no face loaded the measurement is 0, so a fitted label reads 0 and a
 fitted button 16, and an unfitted one keeps its number. The explicit row is
 the one the old rule got wrong: `Hello` guesses 40, and an author who pins
 40 meant 40, where the rule that compared the width to the guess replaced it.

  fit : WidgetNode -> Integer
  fit (n) = (comp-fit-node n gfont-none 1).wn-min-w

  report : Text, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  report (name) (got) (want) = print-line-uni (name & " " & integer-to-text got & ": " & if got == want then "PASS" else "FAIL")

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let natural = widget-label "a" "Hello"
    in let pinned = widget-set-min (widget-label "b" "Hello") 40 20
    in let tall = widget-set-min-h (widget-label "c" "Hello") 20
    in let button = widget-button "d" "Go"
    in act
      report "a natural label is fitted" (fit natural) 0
      report "an explicit width equal to the guess survives" (fit pinned) 40
      report "a height-only pin keeps the fit" (fit tall) 0
      report "a natural button is fitted" (fit button) 16
    end
  end
